Here is the **complete step-by-step guide** to install and run a Node.js project with Express using just one file.

---

# ✅ 1️⃣ Install Node.js

Download and install Node.js from;

👉 [https://nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org)

After installing, check it:

```bash
node -v
npm -v
```

If versions appear, you're ready.

---

# ✅ 2️⃣ Create Project Folder

```bash
mkdir myapp
cd myapp
```

---

# ✅ 3️⃣ Initialize Node Project.

```bash
npm init -y
```

This creates `package.json`.

---

# ✅ 4️⃣ Install Express

```bash
npm install express
```

---

# ✅ 5️⃣ Create Single File `server.js`

Create a file named:

```
server.js
```

Paste this code inside:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

const PORT = 3000;

// Middleware
app.use(express.json());

// Home route
app.get('/', (req, res) => {
    res.send('Server is running 🚀');
});

// Simple API route
app.get('/api', (req, res) => {
    res.json({ message: "Hello from API" });
});

// Start server
app.listen(PORT, () => {
    console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

---

# ✅ 6️⃣ Run The Server

```bash
node server.js
```

You should see:

```
Server running at http://localhost:3000
```

---

# ✅ 7️⃣ Open in Browser

Go to:

```
http://localhost:3000
```

---

# 🔥 Done!

You now have a working Node.js + Express server in **one file**.
